      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "bbox": [
            0.022,
            0.608,
            0.047,
            0.88
          ],
          "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.082,
            0.884,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": "Using these substances can cause serious health problems, such as breathing difficulties, memory loss, and damage to the lungs (Fig. 6.5), depending on the substance. To stay healthy, it is important to completely avoid these substances and make healthy choices instead. It is important to remain firm and confident in your decision to say ‘NO’."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.195,
            0.884,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": "The first step to overcoming addiction is seeking help and support from family and friends, and talking to trusted people, such as parents or teachers. Counselling and medical advice can also be helpful in handling such situations. Remember, your health and your future are in your hands—choose wisely!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.278,
            0.311,
            0.523,
            0.332
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Science and Society"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.278,
            0.336,
            0.588,
            0.356
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.402,
            0.261,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.277,
            0.357,
            0.862,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": "The Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan was launched by the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment, Government of India. It intends to reach out to the masses and spread awareness on the issue of avoiding substance abuse through active participation of the youth, women, and the community. The special focus is on the prevention of substance abuse among early-age children."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.278,
            0.475,
            0.859,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": "The Government has launched a National De-addiction Helpline— 14446, to deal with drug addiction and to help drug addicts."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.537,
            0.859,
            0.562
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "6.5 The ‘Why’ Question for Adolescence"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.37,
            0.601,
            0.713,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": "We now understand the different changes in adolescence and also know some ways to handle it with a sense of responsibility."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.297,
            0.663,
            0.369,
            0.779
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.723,
            0.578,
            0.888,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.7,
            0.682,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": "But I wonder why these changes occur at this stage of life!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.789,
            0.885,
            0.938
          ],
          "content": "Many changes in adolescence, including menstruation and other signs of puberty, are mainly due to **hormones**—certain chemicals produced in our bodies. Hormones play a crucial role in regulating various aspects of growth and development, contributing to the proper functioning of the body. They are produced in different parts of the body and are released at an appropriate time in response to signals from the brain. Some hormones influence mood and behaviour."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
